2. TECHNOLOGY NAMING INTEGRITY & NON-RENAMING CLAUSE (ЗАПРЕТ НА ПРИСВОЕНИЕ И ПЕРЕИМЕНОВАНИЕ)
========================================================================================
No person, corporation, research entity, or third party has the right to rebrand, rename, 
plagiarize, or claim original authorship over the core technologies and architectural 
innovations introduced herein by copying or adapting the implementation under a 
different proprietary name. 

Specifically:
  a) The overall architecture must retain the name "Maba" (e.g., "Maba-Sparse", 
     "Maba v1.5", or explicitly "Maba-based / Derived from Maba");
  b) The core architectural mechanisms and sub-technologies:
       - DGDA (Dual-Gated Delta Attention),
       - MABA-SA (Maba Sparse Attention / Three-Stream Superposition),
       - DG-Indexer (Centroid Block-Sparse Indexer & Mean-Max Routing),
       - HCA (Hierarchical Compressed Attention)
     MUST retain their canonical names and conceptual attribution in technical descriptions, 
     documentation, and published architectures. Rebranding these mechanisms under new 
     labels without explicit attribution to Maba is strictly prohibited.

